id: pm-gf5zw8
title: "GH-1219: report truthful package update coverage for skipped and failed checks"
description: Separate runtime activation health from update evidence and report incomplete coverage whenever eligible managed sources are skipped or fail.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-08T07:41:46.288Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-08T10:51:00.106Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-08T10:50:59.560Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-08T10:50:59.560Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "All-skipped npm, mixed checked/skipped, failed and not-checked managed sources report partial update coverage; successful checks and expected builtins retain valid semantics; SDK CLI and isolated installed-package acceptance agree."
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make package freshness claims depend on completed upstream checks
value: Agents can distinguish healthy activation from unknown update status
impact: Prevents false full-coverage receipts after npm or local adoption
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Implemented truthful update-check coverage and availability totals with status-specific remediation; expected unmanaged builtins receive no contradictory adoption advice. A disposable false-full-coverage mutant verifies the gate.
expected_result: "Activation remains distinct from upstream freshness, skipped and failed sources remain partial, and expected unmanaged exemptions apply consistently to remediation."
actual_result: "8581 tests across 645 files passed with zero uncovered counts: statements 63343/63343, branches 48101/48101, functions 13129/13129 and lines 60821/60821. Nine linked PM commands passed. Full static verification, final build/lint/structural/type checks and idle import/startup gates passed with unchanged budgets. Rebuilt npm and Bun consumers passed source-alias snapshots, destination-alias in-place planning, archive activation, compact/full claims and truthful partial freshness. All three source controls prove baseline exit 0 and unsafe-mutant exit 1. Hosted re-review follows the corrective push."
